      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1899 Asa Candler secretly bought land around the lake, turning the area into a Coca‑Cola‑era development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Lake%2C_Atlanta",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1970 opening of the historic East Lake Meadows housing project marked a turning point for the neighborhood’s social fabric.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.atlantamagazine.com/news-culture-articles/5-reasons-to-love-east-lake/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The East Lake Golf Club, opened in 1904, hosts PGA’s annual Tour Championship and sits beside the lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Lake%2C_Atlanta",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the 1990s, activists founded the East Lake Foundation to reverse a high crime rate and spark community renewal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
